6. Our Process
Building a successful chatbot requires more than writing code — it requires a structured, collaborative process that keeps your business goals at the center of every decision. Here's how our chatbot development process works, from first conversation to long-term optimization.
Step 1: Discovery and Requirement Gathering
We begin with an in-depth discovery session to understand your business, your customers, and the specific problems you want the chatbot to solve. This includes reviewing existing support data, common customer questions, current workflows, and your technical environment. The output of this phase is a clear project scope, success metrics, and a recommended chatbot architecture.
Step 2: Conversation Design and Use Case Mapping
Before any development begins, our conversation design team maps out the dialogue flows — including primary use cases, edge cases, fallback strategies, and tone of voice. We create user journey maps and sample dialogue scripts, which we review with you to make sure the bot's "personality" and logic align with your brand.
Step 3: Platform and Technology Selection
Based on your requirements — budget, timeline, complexity, channels, and integrations — we recommend the right combination of technologies, whether that's a leading NLP platform like Dialogflow or Rasa, a generative AI/LLM-based architecture, or a hybrid approach.
Step 4: Prototype and Proof of Concept
For more complex projects, we often build a working prototype covering core use cases. This allows you to interact with a real, functioning version of the chatbot early in the process, gather internal feedback, and validate the approach before full-scale development begins.
Step 5: Development and Integration
Our development team builds out the full chatbot, including NLP training, integration with your CRM, helpdesk, e-commerce platform, or internal systems, and the underlying infrastructure needed to support your expected conversation volume.
Step 6: Training the AI Model
We train the chatbot's underlying model using your historical data, FAQs, product catalogs, and support transcripts (where available), ensuring it understands your specific terminology, products, and customer language patterns — not just generic conversation patterns.
Step 7: Quality Assurance and Testing
Every chatbot goes through rigorous testing, including:
Functional testing (does each intent and integration work correctly?)
Conversation flow testing (does the dialogue feel natural and logical?)
Edge case and stress testing (how does it handle unexpected input or high volume?)
Security testing (is sensitive data properly protected?)
Cross-channel testing (does it work consistently across every deployment channel?)
Step 8: User Acceptance Testing (UAT)
Before going live, we invite your team to test the chatbot in a staging environment, gather feedback, and request any final adjustments to flows, tone, or functionality.
Step 9: Deployment and Launch
Once approved, we deploy the chatbot to your chosen channels — website, mobile app, messaging platforms, or voice assistants — with careful monitoring during the initial launch window to catch and resolve any issues quickly.
Step 10: Monitoring, Analytics, and Optimization
After launch, we closely monitor conversation analytics to identify gaps, common fallback points, and opportunities for improvement. We continually refine intents, expand the knowledge base, and adjust conversation flows based on real user behavior.
Step 11: Ongoing Support and Scaling
As your business evolves, so does your chatbot. We provide ongoing support packages that include regular updates, new feature additions, expanded integrations, additional language support, and scaling the infrastructure as conversation volume grows.
